libcamera: software_isp: keep highlights clipped in every channel white

The GPU debayer applies the white balance gains to each channel and then
saturates it at the sensor range. Under warm light the red gain falls below
1 (0.72 under a salt lamp on the OnePlus 7 Pro), so a lamp clipped in all
three channels came out (0.72, 1, 1): cyan. Where every channel clipped the
colour is unknown, so it now stays white at the brightest balanced level,
blending in as the last channel nears clipping so there is no edge. The CPU
debayer, which applies the gains through lookup tables, is unchanged.

---
diff --git a/src/libcamera/shaders/bayer_1x_packed.frag b/src/libcamera/shaders/bayer_1x_packed.frag
index 87a8b6b..ad6bf38 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/shaders/bayer_1x_packed.frag
+++ b/src/libcamera/shaders/bayer_1x_packed.frag
@@ -255,8 +255,18 @@ void main(void)
 	 */
 	rgb = (rgb - blacklevel) / (1.0 - blacklevel);
 
-	/* Apply AWB gains, and saturate each channel at sensor range */
-	rgb = clamp(rgb * awb, vec3(0.0), vec3(1.0));
+	/*
+	 * Apply AWB gains, and saturate each channel at sensor range. Where the
+	 * sensor clipped every channel the colour is unknown, so it stays white
+	 * whatever the gains: under warm light a red gain below 1 would turn a
+	 * clipped lamp cyan. The blend starts as the last channel nears clipping,
+	 * so there is no edge.
+	 */
+	vec3 balanced = rgb * awb;
+	float least = min(rgb.r, min(rgb.g, rgb.b));
+	float brightest = max(balanced.r, max(balanced.g, balanced.b));
+	balanced = mix(balanced, vec3(brightest), smoothstep(0.85, 0.98, least));
+	rgb = clamp(balanced, vec3(0.0), vec3(1.0));
 
 	/* Colour Correction Matrix */
 	rgb = ccm * rgb;
diff --git a/src/libcamera/shaders/bayer_unpacked.frag b/src/libcamera/shaders/bayer_unpacked.frag
index 25d2f0e..575e313 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/shaders/bayer_unpacked.frag
+++ b/src/libcamera/shaders/bayer_unpacked.frag
@@ -158,8 +158,18 @@ void main(void) {
      */
     rgb = (rgb - blacklevel) / (1.0 - blacklevel);
 
-    /* Apply AWB gains, and saturate each channel at sensor range */
-    rgb = clamp(rgb * awb, vec3(0.0), vec3(1.0));
+    /*
+     * Apply AWB gains, and saturate each channel at sensor range. Where the
+     * sensor clipped every channel the colour is unknown, so it stays white
+     * whatever the gains: under warm light a red gain below 1 would turn a
+     * clipped lamp cyan. The blend starts as the last channel nears clipping,
+     * so there is no edge.
+     */
+    vec3 balanced = rgb * awb;
+    float least = min(rgb.r, min(rgb.g, rgb.b));
+    float brightest = max(balanced.r, max(balanced.g, balanced.b));
+    balanced = mix(balanced, vec3(brightest), smoothstep(0.85, 0.98, least));
+    rgb = clamp(balanced, vec3(0.0), vec3(1.0));
 
     /* Colour Correction Matrix */
     rgb = ccm * rgb;
